# Dragon's Reach — module contracts

**Read this fully before writing code. Do not change any signature in this file.**
If you believe a signature is wrong, implement it as specified anyway and note the
objection in your final report. Other agents are compiling against it right now.

## Ground rules

- Three.js `r180`, ES modules, Vite. `import * as THREE from 'three'`.
- Units: **1 unit = 1 metre. Y is up.** The dragon is ~1.15 m at the shoulder,
  2.2 m nose to tail-tip. Gravity is `-26 m/s²` (game-feel, not physical).
- **Determinism is mandatory.** Never call `Math.random()`. Take an `Rng` and use
  `rng.fork('your-tag')` for each independent stream, so adding a rock does not
  shift enemy placement.
- **Own only your files.** Never edit a file outside your assigned list. If you
  need something from another module, call its contract.
- Everything you add to the scene must set `castShadow` / `receiveShadow`
  deliberately, and must be disposed in your `dispose()`.
- No network requests, no external asset URLs, no CDN. Everything is generated in
  code or bundled. The build must work fully offline.
- Prefer `InstancedMesh` for anything appearing more than ~20 times. Budget:
  the whole scene should stay under ~450 draw calls.

## Core services (already written — consume, don't edit)

### `src/core/Rng.js`
```js
new Rng(seed)            // .next() .range(a,b) .int(a,b) .bool(p) .pick(arr)
                         // .weighted(items, weights) .shuffle(arr) .gauss(m,sd)
                         // .disc(r) -> [x,y]  .fork(tag) -> Rng
makeNoise2D(rng) -> (x,y)=>[-1,1]      makeNoise3D(rng) -> (x,y,z)=>[-1,1]
fbm2(noise2, x, y, oct, lac, gain)     ridged2(...)      // same args
clamp(v,a,b)  lerp(a,b,t)  smoothstep(e0,e1,x)  damp(a,b,rate,dt)
```
`damp` is the frame-rate-independent smoothing you should use for **all**
easing. Never write `a += (b-a) * 0.1` in an update loop.

### `src/core/Engine.js`
```js
engine.scene, engine.camera, engine.renderer, engine.composer
engine.sun            // THREE.DirectionalLight, the shadow caster
engine.sunDirection   // THREE.Vector3, normalised, points sun -> origin
engine.quality        // { ssao, shadowMap, bloom, smaa, pixelRatio, softShadow }
engine.qualityName    // 'low' | 'medium' | 'high' | 'ultra'
engine.applyBiomeLighting(biome, immediate)
engine.focusShadows(targetVec3, radius)
```

### `src/core/Input.js`
```js
input.move    // THREE.Vector2, x = strafe, y = forward, length <= 1
input.look    // THREE.Vector2, delta this frame (already scaled)
input.down('jump'|'flame'|'charge'|'pause'|'map'|'restart'|'camReset')
input.pressed(action)   // edge
input.released(action)
input.zoomDelta
```

### `src/world/Biomes.js`
```js
BIOMES, BIOME_IDS, getBiome(id), pickBiomeSequence(rng, n), GEM_TIERS
```
A biome object has `ground{base,mid,peak,cliff,sand}`, `foliage{canopyA,canopyB,
canopyC,trunk,grass,flowerA,flowerB}`, `rock{base,accent}`, `sky{zenith,horizon,
ground,sunTint,cloudLit,cloudShadow}`, `sun{color,intensity,elevation,azimuth}`,
`ambient{sky,ground,intensity}`, `fog{color,density}`, `water{shallow,deep,foam}`,
`accent`, `props{...weights}`, `enemies{...weights}`, `audio{scale,root,tempo,warmth}`.

**Every colour you use must come from the biome palette.** Do not hardcode
colours. That is what makes each run read as one coherent place.

### `src/world/Terrain.js` — the ground query
```js
terrain.sampleGround(x, z) -> null | {
  y,          // world-space ground height
  normal,     // THREE.Vector3, unit
  slope,      // radians from vertical, 0 = flat
  island,     // Island instance
  islandId,
  u,          // 0 at island centre, 1 at the rim
